	(text "BUFFERED, unlike the GU04 beside it"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6000 220.9800 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c8507973-0fdc-61c5-0bb6-cc27427727b6")
	)
	(text_box "WHY THE 74LVC1G34 HERE AND THE 74LVC1GU04 NEXT DOOR.\nThey are opposites on purpose.  The squarer needs the UNBUFFERED GU04 because it\nis run inside a 1M feedback loop at its own threshold, and one gain stage in\nthat loop cannot oscillate while three can.\nEverything after it wants the exact opposite: no feedback, no linear region,\njust the fastest, stiffest edge available into fourteen flip-flop clock inputs.\nThat is the BUFFERED G34 - three cascaded stages, ~30 ohm output, and an input\nslew-rate limit in its Recommended Operating Conditions that the squarer's clean\nedge already satisfies.  Using a GU04 here would give soft edges and multiply\nevery flip-flop's threshold mismatch straight into skew."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8000 166.3700 0)
		(size 139.7000 29.2100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fde3e45b-d956-12e8-6612-93d951e3040a")
	)
	(text_box "HELPER SKEW ENTERS AT FULL SCALE, 1:1.  A delay d in one channel's helper branch\nshifts that channel's beat by d x N, which referred back to the input is d.\nOnly DIFFERENTIAL drift survives: a constant is a per-channel calibration the\nnull test removes, and a shift common to all fourteen branches cancels exactly.\nSo the copper barely matters, and it is worth doing the arithmetic rather than\nreflexively length-matching.  FR4 carries about 6.9 ps/mm and its delay tempco\nis 50-100 ppm/degC, so a branch MISMATCH of 100 mm - the worst this board could\nproduce - drifts 0.7 ps over a 10 degC swing, against a 12.3 ps single-shot\nresolution.  Match the branches to 10 mm because it is free, not to 1 mm; the\nlength itself is a per-channel constant the null test removes.\nSILICON is the whole problem, which is why the four second-stage buffers have to\nbe physically ADJACENT so their tempcos track.  That is the layout constraint,\nand it is the only one on this sheet that is tight."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.7200 166.3700 0)
		(size 121.9200 36.8300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 220 220 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4e064c6-6dfb-b4f2-cf64-469b8c6e69d9")
	)
